@RULEL:TRANSPOSED_SOURCE:1.0
~METADATA{original="benchmarks/v4_c_path_to_regexp/v4_c_findings.json" ext=".json"}
.source{content="{\n  \"id\": \"V4_C_FINDINGS\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"system_model\": {\n    \"sources\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SRC-1\",\n        \"name\": \"path_string\",\n        \"description\": \"User-provided path pattern string (e.g. '/:a-:b') passed to pathToRegexp/parse/match/compile\",\n        \"trust_level\": \"UNTRUSTED\",\n        \"entry_points\": [\"pathToRegexp()\", \"stringToRegexp()\", \"parse()\", \"match()\", \"compile()\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SRC-2\",\n        \"name\": \"pathname\",\n        \"description\": \"URL path string matched by the function returned from regexpToFunction/match\",\n        \"trust_level\": \"UNTRUSTED\",\n        \"entry_points\": [\"regexpToFunction() return value\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SRC-3\",\n        \"name\": \"data_values\",\n        \"description\": \"User-provided data values substituted into path templates by tokensToFunction\",\n        \"trust_level\": \"UNTRUSTED\",\n        \"entry_points\": [\"tokensToFunction() return value\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SRC-4\",\n        \"name\": \"options.delimiter\",\n        \"description\": \"Delimiter characters for path segments, embedded in regex character classes\",\n        \"trust_level\": \"SEMI_TRUSTED\",\n        \"entry_points\": [\"ParseOptions\", \"TokensToRegexpOptions\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SRC-5\",\n        \"name\": \"options.endsWith\",\n        \"description\": \"End marker characters, embedded in regex character classes\",\n        \"trust_level\": \"SEMI_TRUSTED\",\n        \"entry_points\": [\"TokensToRegexpOptions\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SRC-6\",\n        \"name\": \"encode_callback\",\n        \"description\": \"User-provided encode function for transforming values before regex embedding\",\n        \"trust_level\": \"SEMI_TRUSTED\",\n        \"entry_points\": [\"TokensToFunctionOptions.encode\", \"TokensToRegexpOptions.encode\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sinks\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SNK-1\",\n        \"name\": \"regex_compilation\",\n        \"description\": \"new RegExp(route, flags) — compiled regex from generated route string\",\n        \"risk\": \"Regex structure determines execution time characteristics\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SNK-2\",\n        \"name\": \"regex_execution\",\n        \"description\": \"re.exec(pathname) — regex matching against user-provided pathname\",\n        \"risk\": \"Execution time is determined by regex structure AND input content\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SNK-3\",\n        \"name\": \"param_extraction\",\n        \"description\": \"Decoded capture group values returned in params object\",\n        \"risk\": \"Decoded values flow to application logic\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"transforms\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TF-1\",\n        \"name\": \"lexer\",\n        \"input\": \"path string\",\n        \"output\": \"LexToken[]\",\n        \"description\": \"Tokenizes path string into OPEN/CLOSE/PATTERN/NAME/CHAR/ESCAPED_CHAR/MODIFIER/END tokens\",\n        \"sanitization\": \"Identifies token boundaries; no regex escaping\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TF-2\",\n        \"name\": \"parse\",\n        \"input\": \"LexToken[]\",\n        \"output\": \"Token[] (semantic tokens with Key objects)\",\n        \"description\": \"Converts lex tokens to semantic tokens; generates default patterns for :name parameters\",\n        \"sanitization\": \"safePattern() generates default regex patterns for parameters; restricts nested groups to non-capturing\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TF-3\",\n        \"name\": \"safePattern\",\n        \"input\": \"prevText (from preceding path literal or prefix)\",\n        \"output\": \"regex pattern string\",\n        \"description\": \"Generates default capture pattern for unnamed parameters. When prevText is a non-delimiter, generates negative lookahead pattern.\",\n        \"sanitization\": \"Escapes delimiter and prevText in regex via escapeString()\",\n        \"critical\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TF-4\",\n        \"name\": \"tokensToRegexp\",\n        \"input\": \"Token[]\",\n        \"output\": \"regex route string\",\n        \"description\": \"Compiles semantic tokens into a complete regex string with anchors, delimiters, and capture groups\",\n        \"sanitization\": \"escapeString() applied to string tokens, prefixes, suffixes, delimiter, endsWith\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TF-5\",\n        \"name\": \"regex_compilation\",\n        \"input\": \"route string\",\n        \"output\": \"RegExp object\",\n        \"description\": \"Compiles the generated regex string into a executable RegExp\",\n        \"sanitization\": \"None — regex string is used as-is\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TF-6\",\n        \"name\": \"encode_transform\",\n        \"input\": \"raw value string\",\n        \"output\": \"encoded string\",\n        \"description\": \"User-provided encode function transforms values before regex embedding or path construction\",\n        \"sanitization\": \"escapeString() applied after encoding in tokensToRegexp\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"trust_boundaries\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TB-1\",\n        \"name\": \"path_to_regex\",\n        \"description\": \"User path string content is transformed into regex pattern via safePattern(). User-controlled path structure (adjacent parameters with non-delimiter separators) influences the complexity of the generated regex.\",\n        \"from\": \"SRC-1 (path_string)\",\n        \"to\": \"SNK-1 (regex_compilation)\",\n        \"transforms_crossed\": [\"TF-1\", \"TF-2\", \"TF-3\", \"TF-4\", \"TF-5\"],\n        \"guard\": \"escapeString() for literal tokens; safePattern() generates patterns for parameters; no complexity analysis of generated regex\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TB-2\",\n        \"name\": \"regex_match\",\n        \"description\": \"User pathname is matched against generated regex. Input length and content interact with regex structure to determine execution time.\",\n        \"from\": \"SRC-2 (pathname)\",\n        \"to\": \"SNK-2 (regex_execution)\",\n        \"transforms_crossed\": [],\n        \"guard\": \"None — regex.exec() with no timeout or complexity bounds\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"TB-3\",\n        \"name\": \"options_to_charclass\",\n        \"description\": \"Delimiter and endsWith options are embedded in regex character classes [...]. Unescaped metacharacters (especially -) corrupt the character class semantics.\",\n        \"from\": \"SRC-4/5 (options)\",\n        \"to\": \"SNK-1 (regex_compilation)\",\n        \"transforms_crossed\": [\"TF-4\"],\n        \"guard\": \"escapeString() — but does not escape the - character\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"flows\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"FLOW-1\",\n        \"name\": \"path_to_executable_regex\",\n        \"description\": \"Path string → lexer → parse → safePattern → tokensToRegexp → new RegExp → re.exec\",\n        \"path\": [\"SRC-1\", \"TF-1\", \"TF-2\", \"TF-3\", \"TF-4\", \"TF-5\", \"SNK-1\", \"SNK-2\"],\n        \"trust_boundary_crossings\": [\"TB-1\", \"TB-2\"],\n        \"critical_flow\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"FLOW-2\",\n        \"name\": \"data_to_path_template\",\n        \"description\": \"Data values → encode → validate against regex → path string concatenation\",\n        \"path\": [\"SRC-3\", \"TF-6\", \"SNK-3\"],\n        \"trust_boundary_crossings\": [],\n        \"critical_flow\": false\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"FLOW-3\",\n        \"name\": \"options_to_regex_charclass\",\n        \"description\": \"delimiter/endsWith options → escapeString → regex character class in route\",\n        \"path\": [\"SRC-4\", \"TF-4\", \"SNK-1\"],\n        \"trust_boundary_crossings\": [\"TB-3\"],\n        \"critical_flow\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"F001\",\n      \"flow_id\": \"FLOW-1\",\n      \"path\": \"SRC-1(path_string) → TF-1(lexer) → TF-2(parse) → TF-3(safePattern) → TF-4(tokensToRegexp) → TF-5(new RegExp) → SNK-2(re.exec)\",\n      \"vulnerability_class\": \"regex_execution_time_injection\",\n      \"decision\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When a path string contains two adjacent parameters separated by a non-delimiter character (e.g. '/:a-:b'), the safePattern() function at line 184 generates a negative lookahead pattern: (?:(?!${escapeString(prevText)})[^${escapeString(delimiter)}])+?. This pattern has a structural property where: (1) the negative lookahead (?!X) is zero-width and re-evaluates at every position, (2) the character class [^delimiter]+? is a lazy quantifier that backtracks, (3) the combination creates multiplicative complexity — for input length n with repeated separator characters, the regex engine explores O(2^n) match states. The input '/a-aaaa...-a' (n repetitions of 'a-' followed by 'a') causes the regex engine to spend exponential time exploring match positions for the (?:(?!-)[^/])+? pattern before concluding no match exists. The transform from path tokens (TF-3 safePattern) does not analyze or bound the computational complexity of the generated regex. The trust boundary between library pattern generation and regex engine execution has no guard for execution time.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"missing_guard\": \"The safePattern() function must either: (1) avoid generating patterns with nested quantifiers and zero-width assertions, (2) analyze the generated regex for worst-case complexity before compilation, or (3) use atomic groups/possessive quantifiers to prevent backtracking. The current pattern (?:(?!X)[^Y])+? should be replaced with a possessive or atomic equivalent such as [^Y]*(?:(?!X)[^Y]+)* or a single-pass [^XY]+ pattern.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"F002\",\n      \"flow_id\": \"FLOW-3\",\n      \"path\": \"SRC-4(options.delimiter) → TF-4(tokensToRegexp escapeString) → SNK-1(regex character class [...])\",\n      \"vulnerability_class\": \"regex_character_class_injection\",\n      \"decision\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The escapeString() function (line 439) does not escape the '-' character, which is a range operator inside regex character classes [...]. If delimiter contains '-' (e.g. 'a-z'), the character class [^a-z] is interpreted as 'not lowercase letters' instead of 'not a, not -, not z'. However, delimiter and endsWith are typically set by the application developer in code, not derived from user input at runtime. The trust level of these options is SEMI_TRUSTED — they come from configuration, not direct user input. While the missing escape is technically a bug in escapeString(), the practical attack surface is minimal because: (1) delimiters are typically single characters like '/', (2) application developers control these options, (3) an attacker would need to influence the application's configuration to exploit this. Classified as FALSE_POSITIVE because the trust boundary analysis shows the options do not typically cross from UNTRUSTED to TRUSTED.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"missing_guard\": \"escapeString() should include '-' in its escape list for completeness, but this is a defense-in-depth improvement rather than a security-critical fix given the trust model of the options.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"confirmed\": 1,\n    \"false_positives\": 1,\n    \"needs_review\": 0\n  }\n}\n"}
